  <div id="sutta">
  
            <h4 id="thag3.8" class="h1">Thag 3:8  Yasoja</h4>
            <div class="verse">
              <p>His limbs knotted</p>
              <p>like a kālā plant,</p>
              <p>his body lean</p>
              <p>&amp; lined with veins,</p>
              <p>knowing moderation</p>
              <p>in food &amp; drink:</p>
              <p class="v2">the man of undaunted heart.</p>
              <div class="verse-add">
                <p>Touched by gnats</p>
                <p>&amp; horseflies</p>
                <p class="v2">in the wilds,</p>
                <p class="v2">the great wood,</p>
                <p>like an elephant</p>
                <p>at the head of a battle:</p>
                <p class="v2">He, mindful,</p>
                <p class="v2">should stay there,</p>
                <p class="v2">endure.</p>
              </div><!--end verse-add-->
              <div class="verse-add">
                <p>One alone is like Brahmā,</p>
                <p>two, like devas,</p>
                <p>three, like a village,</p>
                <p>more than that:</p>
                <p class="v2">a hullabaloo.</p>
              </div><!--end verse-add-->
            </div><!--end verse-->
            <p class="seealso">See also: <a href="../Ud/ud3_3.html">Ud 3:3</a>; <a href="../StNp/StNp4_16.html">Sn 4:16</a></p><!--end seealso-->
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
